# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BRING YOUR OWN DISC. The game executable and any disc image stay out of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
disk/*
!disk/.gitignore
!disk/README.md
*.bin
*.cue
*.iso
*.img
LSD - Dream Emulator*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED. splat rewrites all of this on every `make extract`; committing it
# would turn regenerated disassembly into merge conflicts and let stale files
# accumulate invisibly (southpark-decomp round 79 found 1604 stale against 992
# live). If a segment ever holds assembly that was NEVER compiled from C, give
# it splat's `hasm` type, commit it, and add a negation here -- an `hasm` file
# is authored source, splat only writes it when missing, and annotating it is
# the whole point of the category.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
asm/
build/
expected/
*.ld
config/undefined_funcs_auto.*.txt
config/undefined_syms_auto.*.txt
ctx.c
ctx.c.m2c

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TOOLCHAIN. Fetched or built by tools/setup.sh, never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO TRAILING SLASHES ON THESE. A trailing slash makes a pattern match only a
# DIRECTORY. In the main checkout these are real directories, so `tools/gcc263/`
# ignored them fine -- but tools/setup-worktree.sh gives every worktree SYMLINKS
# to them, and a symlink is not a directory, so all seven showed up as untracked
# in every runner worktree. That silently disables the honesty check in
# docs/PARALLEL-RUNS.md 3b: `git status --porcelain` can never be empty, so the
# head cannot distinguish a runner that committed its work from one that did
# not. The slashless form matches both spellings.
.venv
tools/binutils
tools/splat
tools/asm-differ
tools/m2c
tools/maspsx
tools/decomp-permuter
tools/gcc263
tools/psyq-obj-parser
permuter-work
# Seed scaffolds a runner hands the permuter. Generated working state, same
# as permuter-work, and NOT the durable record: a preserved body belongs
# inlined in its match report, never as a path into an ignored directory
# (PARALLEL-RUNS collision rule 2). Untracked and unignored, this directory
# made it impossible for a runner using the permuter to ever report the
# empty `git status --porcelain` the runner protocol requires -- which is a
# check the round relies on, so it must not be the thing that cries wolf.
permuter-seeds
# `permuter.py --debug` writes these into the CURRENT directory, not into the
# permuter dir. MATCHING-GUIDE now tells everyone to run --debug first (a
# scaffold whose base score does not match the match report is scoring the
# wrong thing), so they will keep reappearing in the repo root.
debug_source.c
debug_compiled_object.o

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vscode/
scratchpad/

# Per-operator permission grants. `additionalDirectories` takes ABSOLUTE
# paths, and a worktree path is derived from the basename of whoever's
# checkout it is, so a committed entry would be wrong in every clone but
# one. PARALLEL-RUNS.md has always described this file as gitignored; it
# was not, until round 12 went to write it and found out.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PSY-Q SDK. Bring your own disc, exactly like disk/. sdk/ holds the user's
# SDK discs and everything unpacked from them; lib/ holds the converted Sony
# objects the build links (splat `o` segments). config/psyq-objects.txt is the
# committed manifest that regenerates lib/ from sdk/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sdk/*
!sdk/README.md
lib/
